description:
Design a 4-input priority multiplexer that outputs one of the four input signals based on priority levels. The circuit assesses the inputs in pairs, first grouping them to determine which pair has a value, and then further processing to select the highest-priority signal: input 3 has the highest priority, followed by input 2, then input 1, and finally input 0, if none of the higher-priority inputs are active. The module ensures that only one output is asserted based on these priority levels.
module top_module(
    input [3:0] in,
    output reg out
);

