Design a 4-to-16 line decoder that takes a 4-bit binary input and produces a corresponding 16-bit output. When the enable signal is active, the decoder output will have a single bit set high (1) corresponding to the value of the binary input, while all other bits remain low (0). If the enable signal is not active, the decoder output will be all low, effectively rendering the decoder inactive.
