description:
Design a 3-bit wide priority encoder that takes an 8-bit input. The output indicates the position of the highest-order bit set to 1 in the input, with priority given to the most significant bit. If none of the input bits are active, the output defaults to the maximum binary value (3'b111).
module top_module(
    input [7:0] in,
    output reg [2:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [7:0] in,
    output reg [2:0] out
);always @(*) begin
    casez(in)
        8'b00000001: out = 3'b000;
        8'b00000010: out = 3'b001;
        8'b00000100: out = 3'b010;
        8'b00001000: out = 3'b011;
        8'b00010000: out = 3'b100;
        8'b00100000: out = 3'b101;
        8'b01000000: out = 3'b110;
        8'b10000000: out = 3'b111;
        default: out = 3'b111;
    endcase
end

endmodule

