Design a power good indicator circuit that determines the operational status of power supplies based on the inputs A1, A2, B1, and B2. The module uses two OR gates to evaluate the state of the input signals, and generates a 'power good' output which is then buffered to drive the VPB and VNB outputs. The output indicates if at least one input from A1, A2, B1, or B2 is in a good state, ensuring that the module can signal appropriate power availability at the outputs while maintaining internal logic states.
